# Glue stores every tracked file as text with LF endings.
#
# Why this file exists: `gofmt -w` writes LF on every platform (and drops UTF-8
# BOMs). On a worktree checked out with CRLF (Git for Windows defaults to
# `core.autocrlf=true`), every file gofmt rewrites keeps its CRLF-era index stat,
# so `git status` reports it as "modified — LF will be replaced by CRLF" while
# `git diff` shows no content change at all. That produced a 249-file
# false-positive storm over 70 real changes. Declaring `eol=lf` here makes LF the
# single expected form for both the repository and the working tree, so the false
# positives cannot come back.
#
# The repository already stores LF for all 482 tracked blobs, so this declaration
# needs no renormalization commit.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts (installer output, downloaded archives, icons) must never be
# converted or diffed as text.
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.zip   binary
*.7z    binary
*.gz    binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.woff2 binary
